WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.469 --> 00:00:04.580
We're bringing up the holographic schematics
and outlining how Tony Stark goes from a genius

00:00:04.580 --> 00:00:09.100
weapons designer with no heart to Iron Man,
a self-sacrificing superhero with a heart

00:00:09.100 --> 00:00:09.600
of gold.

00:00:09.860 --> 00:00:13.140
This is the entire Iron Man MCU timeline,
finally explained.

00:00:13.560 --> 00:00:16.180
Consider it all the proof you need that Tony
Stark has a heart.

00:00:16.840 --> 00:00:18.520
So let's get down to brass tacks, shall we?

00:00:18.880 --> 00:00:21.460
Tony Stark basically comes out of the womb
a genius.

00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:23.520
At age 4, he builds a circuit board.

00:00:23.680 --> 00:00:25.640
At age 6, he builds a V8 engine.

00:00:25.740 --> 00:00:31.199
By 17 years old, he graduates summa cum laude
at MIT, and seems poised to take over Stark

00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:34.700
Industries whenever his genius father Howard
feels ready to pass the buck.

00:00:34.920 --> 00:00:39.420
Unfortunately, after Howard's assassination
in 1991 by a brainwashed Bucky Barnes who

00:00:39.430 --> 00:00:43.690
was working as the Winter Soldier his partner
Obadiah Stane takes over Stark Industries

00:00:43.690 --> 00:00:46.700
until Tony turns 21 and takes back his company.

00:00:46.870 --> 00:00:50.920
From there, it's a wild ride of building new
technology and weapons for the American military

00:00:50.920 --> 00:00:54.760
for the next decade, while ticking off just
about everyone in the scientific community.

00:00:54.820 --> 00:00:59.300
When viewers officially meet Tony Stark in
2008's Iron Man, he's at a weapons exhibition

00:00:59.310 --> 00:01:04.180
in Afghanistan to showcase "The Jericho,"
a missile system that uses repulsor technology

00:01:04.180 --> 00:01:05.180
to increase effectiveness.

00:01:05.440 --> 00:01:09.360
"For your consideration… the Jericho."

00:01:14.480 --> 00:01:19.020
On the way back from a successful presentation,
Tony is kidnapped by a terrorist organization

00:01:19.030 --> 00:01:22.600
known as the Ten Rings that want him to build
them their own Jericho missile.

00:01:22.600 --> 00:01:26.530
The explosive kidnapping leaves Tony with
some shrapnel buried near his heart, kept

00:01:26.530 --> 00:01:30.280
temporarily at bay with the use of an electromagnet
powered by a car battery.

00:01:30.450 --> 00:01:35.060
With his fellow captive Ho Yinsen, Tony upgrades
the electromagnet in his chest into an arc

00:01:35.060 --> 00:01:36.240
reactor to keep his heart safe.

00:01:36.240 --> 00:01:40.560
Then he builds his first suit of armor: the
Mark I a clunky mobile suit packed full of

00:01:40.560 --> 00:01:42.940
weaponry which he dons to escape the Ten Rings.

00:01:42.940 --> 00:01:45.240
Sadly, Ho Yinsen doesn't survive the escape.

00:01:45.560 --> 00:01:49.040
With his dying breath, he begs Tony to do
something important with his life.

00:01:49.940 --> 00:01:50.920
"Thank you for saving me."

00:01:51.740 --> 00:01:56.520
"Don't waste it — don't waste your life."

00:01:56.840 --> 00:01:59.950
Nothing like a near-death experience and the
tragic passing of the dude who saved your

00:01:59.950 --> 00:02:02.140
life to really shake up your core principles,
huh?

00:02:02.520 --> 00:02:07.180
"Effective immediately, I am shutting down
the weapons manufacturing division of Stark

00:02:07.180 --> 00:02:07.680
International."

00:02:07.860 --> 00:02:11.840
. Obadiah's against the decision and so is
Tony's best friend Colonel James "Rhodey"

00:02:11.840 --> 00:02:12.340
Rhodes.

00:02:12.440 --> 00:02:16.640
Unfortunately, Tony's new conscience comes
with a cost; the board of Stark Industries

00:02:16.650 --> 00:02:21.480
basically ousts Tony and it turns out that
Obadiah's been playing both sides, both in

00:02:21.480 --> 00:02:24.220
terms of the Stark Industries board and the
global weapons market.

00:02:24.310 --> 00:02:27.880
He actually led the board's betrayal, and
he's been selling Stark Industries tech to

00:02:27.880 --> 00:02:29.480
terrorist groups the whole time.

00:02:29.700 --> 00:02:33.720
Without actual control over Stark Industries
and knowing that plenty of his tech is already

00:02:33.720 --> 00:02:37.810
out in the world, Tony upgrades his Iron Man
suit to be sleeker and more colorful, and

00:02:37.810 --> 00:02:41.240
embarks on a quest to take down any terrorist
groups using his weapons.

00:02:41.260 --> 00:02:45.440
After a successful mission, Tony makes a plan
with his secretary, Pepper Potts, to hack

00:02:45.440 --> 00:02:48.680
into Stark Industries and find out where the
rest of his weapons have gone.

00:02:48.860 --> 00:02:53.680
However, Obadiah incapacitates Tony, steals
the arc reactor in his chest, and places it

00:02:53.680 --> 00:02:56.580
in a suit of his own design that's inspired
by Tony's first one.

00:02:56.700 --> 00:02:58.060
Only… his is bigger.

00:02:58.340 --> 00:02:59.260
A lot bigger.

00:03:03.480 --> 00:03:05.000
"I love this suit!"

00:03:05.320 --> 00:03:09.280
Tony replaces his missing arc reactor with
the prototype that he'd saved from the desert

00:03:09.280 --> 00:03:12.120
and suits up to battle against Obadiah's "Iron
Monger."

00:03:12.120 --> 00:03:16.170
He defeats Obadiah with some help from Pepper
of course saves the day, and then announces

00:03:16.170 --> 00:03:18.480
to the world that there's no secret identity
needed:

00:03:22.440 --> 00:03:23.520
"I am Iron Man."

00:03:27.580 --> 00:03:31.960
While Tony's onstage admitting that he really
is Iron Man, half a world away, Anton Vanko

00:03:31.960 --> 00:03:35.960
passes away after telling his son Ivan that
Tony's life should have been his.

00:03:35.960 --> 00:03:40.200
Ivan uses an old blueprint of the arc reactor
designed by his father and Howard Stark in

00:03:40.200 --> 00:03:42.380
order to build a replica of the super-battery.

00:03:42.769 --> 00:03:46.920
Six months later, Tony's turned his newfound
superhero celebrity into an excuse to bring

00:03:46.930 --> 00:03:50.870
back the Stark Expo, as well as take credit
for basically every good thing that's happened

00:03:50.870 --> 00:03:52.480
in America since Iron Man appeared.

00:03:52.680 --> 00:03:56.540
Predictably, Tony's subpoenaed to appear in
front of Congress to defend his right to bear

00:03:56.550 --> 00:03:57.840
the world's biggest armory.

00:03:57.840 --> 00:04:00.740
"... if your priority was actually the well-being
of the American citizens — "

00:04:00.740 --> 00:04:04.760
"No, my priority is to get the Iron Man weapon
turned over to the people of the United States

00:04:04.760 --> 00:04:05.480
of America."

00:04:05.480 --> 00:04:06.400
"Well… you can forget it."

00:04:06.760 --> 00:04:10.750
Tony talks his way out, but he learns that
Justin Hammer and Hammer Industries are trying

00:04:10.750 --> 00:04:14.200
to fill the void left by Stark Industries
after they left the weapons game… which

00:04:14.420 --> 00:04:18.280
includes trying to copy the Iron Man suit
and failing pretty spectacularly.

00:04:18.400 --> 00:04:22.220
Meanwhile, Tony's got problems of his own:
he's suffering from palladium poisoning from

00:04:22.220 --> 00:04:23.900
the continued use of his arc reactor.

00:04:24.020 --> 00:04:29.020
Tony names Pepper the new CEO of Stark Industries,
while Ivan finishes his arc reactor-powered

00:04:29.020 --> 00:04:29.840
Whiplash outfit.

00:04:30.020 --> 00:04:34.300
Ivan attacks Tony during a race in Monaco,
but Tony's able to suit up and defeat him.

00:04:34.300 --> 00:04:38.340
Justin Hammer gets Ivan out of jail, and the
two agree to team up to take down Tony Stark

00:04:38.400 --> 00:04:39.520
and Stark Industries.

00:04:39.640 --> 00:04:42.980
"You need my resources someone behind you.

00:04:43.340 --> 00:04:43.960
A benefactor.

00:04:44.960 --> 00:04:45.960
I'd like to be that guy."

00:04:49.020 --> 00:04:53.200
Suffering from palladium poisoning and flush
from his victory over Whiplash, Tony goes

00:04:53.200 --> 00:04:55.290
off the deep end during his birthday party.

00:04:55.400 --> 00:04:59.540
He puts on the Iron Man suit as a party trick
and starts blasting away, only for Rhodey

00:04:59.550 --> 00:05:03.509
who's looking a teensy bit different, this
time around to show up in another one of Tony's

00:05:03.509 --> 00:05:04.340
suits to try and stop him.

00:05:06.480 --> 00:05:07.320
"Get out."

00:05:09.580 --> 00:05:13.740
Tony and Rhodey battle it out to a draw, and
Rhodey flies off to give the "War Machine"

00:05:13.740 --> 00:05:14.820
suit to the U.S. military.

00:05:15.000 --> 00:05:18.400
Hammer gets the job of outfitting it with
new weapons, while Nick Fury, the head of

00:05:18.400 --> 00:05:22.240
S.H.I.E.L.D., gives Tony a firm talking to
about how he needs to grow up and figure out

00:05:22.240 --> 00:05:23.920
how to fix his palladium poisoning.

00:05:24.060 --> 00:05:28.080
After viewing a heartfelt recording from his
father, Tony figures out that Howard had designed

00:05:28.090 --> 00:05:32.430
a replacement for palladium in the '70s, but
lacking the technology to build the new element,

00:05:32.430 --> 00:05:35.080
he buried the design in the schematics for
the Stark Expo.

00:05:35.500 --> 00:05:42.340
"What is and always will be my greatest creation…
is you."

00:05:42.840 --> 00:05:47.199
Tony discovers it, builds the new element,
and upgrades his suit just in time to interrupt

00:05:47.199 --> 00:05:51.250
Ivan's master plan: he's built a fleet of
Iron Man-esque drones for Hammer Industries

00:05:51.250 --> 00:05:55.200
that only he controls, as well as remote control
over Rhodey's War Machine armor.

00:05:55.430 --> 00:05:59.740
With the help of Happy Hogan and Natasha Romanoff,
who had been working undercover at Stark Industries

00:05:59.750 --> 00:06:03.830
under the name Natasha Rushman, Tony frees
Rhodey from Ivan's control, and the two of

00:06:03.830 --> 00:06:05.340
them defeat Whiplash together.

00:06:05.340 --> 00:06:09.680
With the day saved, Rhodey keeps the War Machine
armor, while Tony accepts a role as a consultant

00:06:09.680 --> 00:06:11.600
for the Avengers Initiative from Nick Fury.

00:06:12.320 --> 00:06:16.520
Tony next appears in the post-credits scene
for 2008's The Incredible Hulk which takes

00:06:16.520 --> 00:06:20.870
place around the same time as the events of
Iron Man 2 telling General Thaddeus Ross that

00:06:20.870 --> 00:06:22.060
a "team" is being put together.

00:06:22.430 --> 00:06:27.340
That "team" is the Avengers, which Tony officially
joins in 2012's The Avengers, after Loki steals

00:06:27.340 --> 00:06:29.350
the Tesseract from Project P.E.G.A.S.U.S.

00:06:29.350 --> 00:06:33.040
Tony teams up with Captain America and Black
Widow to capture Loki in Germany.

00:06:33.260 --> 00:06:37.100
After the team nabs Loki, Thor shows up to
scuffle with Cap and Iron Man before agreeing

00:06:37.100 --> 00:06:39.260
to team up against whatever Loki's plotting.

00:06:39.540 --> 00:06:40.860
The team heads to the S.H.I.E.L.D.

00:06:40.860 --> 00:06:44.980
helicarrier, where Tony and Bruce Banner,
a.k.a. the Hulk, get to work analyzing Loki's

00:06:44.980 --> 00:06:46.300
mind-controlling scepter.

00:06:46.440 --> 00:06:50.980
Loki's henchmen including a hypnotized Hawkeye
ambush the Helicarrier, freeing the trickster

00:06:50.990 --> 00:06:53.660
god and sending the Avengers team into disarray.

00:06:53.660 --> 00:06:57.450
The team comes back together just in time
for a massive battle in New York, centered

00:06:57.450 --> 00:07:01.530
around Stark Tower where Loki's attempting
to open a rift to bring in an invading force

00:07:01.530 --> 00:07:02.940
of alien Chitauri warriors.

00:07:03.120 --> 00:07:07.490
The Avengers stem the tide, the World Security
Council launches a nuclear missile, and Iron

00:07:07.490 --> 00:07:11.520
Man drags the missile through the wormhole
into the Chitauri fleet, seemingly sacrificing

00:07:11.520 --> 00:07:13.060
his life to destroy the invaders.

00:07:13.100 --> 00:07:14.720
Luckily, he's totally fine.

00:07:14.960 --> 00:07:15.640
Kinda.

00:07:15.960 --> 00:07:16.460
"Alright.

00:07:16.460 --> 00:07:16.960
Hey!

00:07:17.400 --> 00:07:17.900
Alright.

00:07:17.900 --> 00:07:18.480
Good job, guys.

00:07:19.380 --> 00:07:20.380
Let's just… not come in tomorrow.

00:07:20.860 --> 00:07:22.200
Let's just take a day."

00:07:22.340 --> 00:07:26.360
In Iron Man 3, which takes place six months
after The Avengers, it's revealed that Tony

00:07:26.360 --> 00:07:28.040
Stark is definitely not fine.

00:07:28.300 --> 00:07:31.780
He's nearly crippled with anxiety following
his excursion through the wormhole and the

00:07:31.880 --> 00:07:32.700
Battle of New York.

00:07:32.930 --> 00:07:37.100
In the meantime, he's dealt with his manic
energy by investing in Damage Control, an

00:07:37.110 --> 00:07:40.690
organization originally created by S.H.I.E.L.D.
to store dangerous artifacts, and spending

00:07:40.690 --> 00:07:44.590
his free time building dozens of Iron Man
suits in case he ever needs more firepower

00:07:44.590 --> 00:07:46.400
for a future earth-shattering crisis.

00:07:46.440 --> 00:07:50.680
One obvious crisis that doesn't take long
to pop up is the Mandarin, a mysterious terrorist

00:07:50.680 --> 00:07:53.520
leader who's been supposedly instigating bombings
throughout the world.

00:07:53.680 --> 00:07:55.140
"You know who I am.

00:07:56.540 --> 00:07:57.540
You don't know where I am.

00:07:59.680 --> 00:08:02.140
And you'll never see me coming."

00:08:02.260 --> 00:08:06.120
After Happy Hogan is injured in one of the
Mandarin's bombings, Tony calls the Mandarin

00:08:06.120 --> 00:08:08.660
out which leads to Tony's house getting blown
up.

00:08:08.840 --> 00:08:13.240
Tony flees to Tennessee, where he meets Harley
Keener, a young boy with a gift for engineering.

00:08:13.320 --> 00:08:16.880
Together with Harley, Tony fixes up his suit
and learns where the Mandarin is hiding.

00:08:16.880 --> 00:08:20.810
Unfortunately, there's a bigger game at work:
The Mandarin is just an actor playing a part

00:08:20.810 --> 00:08:25.260
designed by Aldrich Killian and Maya Hansen
to give a narrative for their failed Extremis

00:08:25.260 --> 00:08:25.760
tests.

00:08:25.760 --> 00:08:29.660
After unraveling a conspiracy involving the
vice president and Killian's plot to kill

00:08:29.660 --> 00:08:33.900
the president, Tony, Rhodey, and Pepper are
able to defeat Killian and save the day.

00:08:33.940 --> 00:08:38.159
Tony undergoes heart surgery so he no longer
needs the arc reactor in order to live, and

00:08:38.160 --> 00:08:39.700
seemingly retires from the hero business.

00:08:40.520 --> 00:08:41.520
Haha yeah right!

00:08:41.780 --> 00:08:45.759
Tony Stark doesn't actually end up retiring,
since he's right back in the Avengers lineup

00:08:45.759 --> 00:08:49.980
in 2015's Avengers: Age of Ultron on the hunt
for HYDRA leader Baron Strucker.

00:08:49.980 --> 00:08:54.230
Iron Man flies into the castle where he's
hiding and gets mind-zapped by Wanda Maximoff,

00:08:54.230 --> 00:08:57.520
one of two super-powered siblings groomed
by Strucker for his evil plans.

00:08:57.700 --> 00:09:01.520
While under Wanda's spell, Tony sees a vision
of his fellow Avengers dead and a Chitauri

00:09:01.520 --> 00:09:02.960
army headed for Earth.

00:09:03.180 --> 00:09:07.280
Once he wakes up, Tony does what he always
does when confronted with a possibly terrible

00:09:07.280 --> 00:09:08.980
future: he builds a suit of armor.

00:09:09.200 --> 00:09:13.399
This time, however, it's not a literal suit;
instead, Tony wants to build, quote, "a suit

00:09:13.399 --> 00:09:17.290
of armor around the world," which is basically
an artificial intelligence that can protect

00:09:17.290 --> 00:09:18.160
Earth from anything.

00:09:18.320 --> 00:09:22.700
Tony and Bruce crack the code on making it,
and together, they create the AI dubbed Ultron

00:09:23.000 --> 00:09:24.980
with the help of the Mind Stone in Loki's
scepter.

00:09:25.380 --> 00:09:27.440
Yeah… that's when everything pretty much
falls apart…

00:09:27.980 --> 00:09:28.600
"Who sent you?"

00:09:29.420 --> 00:09:31.680
"I see a suit of armor around the world."

00:09:33.360 --> 00:09:34.060
"Ultron."

00:09:34.440 --> 00:09:35.180
"In the flesh."

00:09:35.220 --> 00:09:39.040
Determining that human beings are the problem
with the Earth, Ultron tries to destroy the

00:09:39.050 --> 00:09:42.119
world with the help of the Strucker children,
Wanda and Pietro.

00:09:42.119 --> 00:09:46.360
The Avengers show up to stop him, of course,
but Wanda unleashes another one of her telepathic

00:09:46.360 --> 00:09:50.410
attacks against nearly the entire team, which
leads to the Hulk going on a rampage that

00:09:50.410 --> 00:09:52.440
only Tony and his Hulkbuster armor can stop.

00:09:52.680 --> 00:09:57.259
After that, it all comes to a head in the
fictional country of Sokovia, as Tony builds

00:09:57.259 --> 00:10:00.829
Vision, yet another artificial intelligence,
using the Mind Stone and his J.A.R.V.I.S.

00:10:00.829 --> 00:10:02.540
program as a personality matrix.

00:10:02.630 --> 00:10:06.860
Together, the Avengers and Vision save the
day, Ultron is blown up, and Tony quits the

00:10:06.860 --> 00:10:08.200
team at the end of the film.

00:10:08.620 --> 00:10:09.360
"I will miss you, Tony."

00:10:10.480 --> 00:10:10.980
"Yeah?

00:10:11.680 --> 00:10:13.820
Well, it's time for me to tap out."

00:10:14.640 --> 00:10:18.380
While the Avengers are doing their business,
Tony's trying to cultivate a new breed of

00:10:18.389 --> 00:10:23.890
entrepreneurs by paying off the tuition fees
of every single MIT student in 2016's Captain

00:10:23.890 --> 00:10:25.060
America: Civil War.

00:10:25.170 --> 00:10:29.000
His generosity comes under a dark cloud, though,
when he runs into Miriam, the mother of a

00:10:29.020 --> 00:10:31.840
young man who died in Sokovia during the Ultron
event.

00:10:32.140 --> 00:10:33.900
"His name was Charlie Spencer.

00:10:37.200 --> 00:10:37.700
You murdered him.

00:10:40.020 --> 00:10:40.520
In Sokovia."

00:10:41.320 --> 00:10:45.699
She reads Tony the riot act about his lack
of responsibility, and when General Ross later

00:10:45.700 --> 00:10:49.860
shows up to suggest that the Avengers come
under the official purview of the United Nations,

00:10:50.020 --> 00:10:50.980
Tony supports it.

00:10:51.300 --> 00:10:55.360
Steve Rogers, however, is very much against
the Sokovia Accords, and the two men struggle

00:10:55.360 --> 00:10:56.860
to reconcile their differences.

00:10:57.020 --> 00:11:02.049
Bucky, the Winter Soldier, is freed from custody
by Helmut Zemo as part of an extremely complicated

00:11:02.049 --> 00:11:05.040
plan to avenge the death of Zemo's own family
in Sokovia.

00:11:05.240 --> 00:11:10.260
Steve gathers a team to help Bucky evade capture,
while Tony gets his own team together, consisting

00:11:10.279 --> 00:11:14.040
of Black Widow, War Machine, Vision, Black
Panther, and Spider-Man.

00:11:14.040 --> 00:11:18.019
A scuffle with Steve's team at the airport
turns serious when War Machine is crippled

00:11:18.019 --> 00:11:21.519
by an errant blast from Vision, which sends
Tony into serious mode.

00:11:21.519 --> 00:11:24.850
He arrests Steve's team minus Bucky and Cap,
who've escaped sends his own team home, and

00:11:24.850 --> 00:11:27.080
pursues Cap and Bucky to Siberia alone.

00:11:27.269 --> 00:11:31.360
Zemo's plan comes to a head when Tony discovers
that his parents actually died at Bucky's

00:11:31.360 --> 00:11:33.460
hand rather than in a car accident.

00:11:33.520 --> 00:11:38.340
After a brutal battle, Cap and Bucky escape,
minus Cap's shield, but Cap gives Tony a cell

00:11:38.350 --> 00:11:42.430
phone with his number on it if a time comes
that they ever need to reunite against a greater

00:11:42.430 --> 00:11:42.920
threat.

00:11:43.040 --> 00:11:44.480
Spoiler alert: They will.

00:11:45.100 --> 00:11:49.300
Two months after the events of Captain America:
Civil War, Tony's biggest headache is fending

00:11:49.300 --> 00:11:51.500
off Peter Parker's desire for his mentorship.

00:11:51.700 --> 00:11:55.720
Peter's increasingly desperate to get Tony's
attention once the younger hero discovers

00:11:55.720 --> 00:11:59.959
that the Vulture, a weapons-dealing supervillain,
has been selling high-tech weaponry he scavenged

00:11:59.960 --> 00:12:01.860
from the wreckage of the Chitauri invasion.

00:12:01.930 --> 00:12:05.780
Iron Man bails Spider-Man out twice, first
with the help of a remote-controlled drone,

00:12:05.799 --> 00:12:10.649
and the second time in person, trying to convince
Peter to slow down and be a local hero before

00:12:10.649 --> 00:12:11.940
looking to join the Avengers.

00:12:12.020 --> 00:12:16.120
After the second time, when Iron Man's intervention
is the only thing that keeps the Staten Island

00:12:16.120 --> 00:12:19.800
ferry from sinking, Tony confiscates the high-tech
suit he'd given Peter.

00:12:20.580 --> 00:12:21.960
"I just — I just wanted to be like you!"

00:12:22.620 --> 00:12:23.760
"And I wanted you to be better.

00:12:25.820 --> 00:12:27.800
OK, it's not working out — I'm gonna need
the suit back."

00:12:28.120 --> 00:12:32.200
Even without the suit, Peter can't help but
be a hero, and he ultimately stops the Vulture

00:12:32.200 --> 00:12:34.000
from stealing a shipment of Stark tech.

00:12:34.180 --> 00:12:38.580
As a reward, Tony gives Peter the offer he's
been begging for: a chance to join the Avengers

00:12:38.580 --> 00:12:40.000
and get a brand new Iron suit.

00:12:40.220 --> 00:12:46.360
"When you're ready, why don't you try that
on, and I'll introduce the world to the newest

00:12:46.360 --> 00:12:49.180
official member of the Avengers: Spider-man."

00:12:49.400 --> 00:12:53.600
Peter surprisingly turns him down, and Tony,
looking for a way to distract the reporters

00:12:53.600 --> 00:12:57.140
from an announcement that's suddenly no longer
happening, proposes to Pepper Potts.

00:12:57.820 --> 00:13:02.020
When Avengers: Infinity War begins, Tony is
happily married to Pepper and having dreams

00:13:02.020 --> 00:13:02.900
about their child.

00:13:03.040 --> 00:13:07.079
Their touchy-feely small-talk is interrupted
when Doctor Strange arrives to request Tony's

00:13:07.079 --> 00:13:11.139
help in repelling the invasion of Thanos'
Black Order, who have come to Earth in search

00:13:11.140 --> 00:13:14.569
of the Infinity Stones that Thanos needs to
wipe out half of the universe.

00:13:19.580 --> 00:13:21.040
"Dude, you're embarrassing me in front of
the wizards."

00:13:21.040 --> 00:13:25.500
Strange and his Time Stone are kidnapped by
Thanos' henchman Ebony Maw; Tony Stark and

00:13:25.500 --> 00:13:30.059
Spider-Man, newly decked out in his Iron Spider
outfit, hitch a ride on Maw's spaceship.

00:13:30.059 --> 00:13:34.420
After freeing Strange and blasting Maw into
space, Tony, Peter, and Doctor Strange head

00:13:34.420 --> 00:13:37.060
to the planet Titan to prep for Thanos' pursuit.

00:13:37.120 --> 00:13:41.740
There, they run into Guardians of the Galaxy
members Peter Quill, Drax, Mantis, and Nebula.

00:13:42.060 --> 00:13:45.780
A plan is hatched… and then Thanos arrives
to turn that careful plan into ashes.

00:13:46.009 --> 00:13:50.119
With the rest of his allies down, Tony uses
the full force of his nano-technology-powered

00:13:50.119 --> 00:13:54.279
suit to draw a single drop of blood from Thanos
before the Mad Titan stabs him through the

00:13:54.280 --> 00:13:55.980
abdomen with Tony's own sword.

00:13:56.180 --> 00:14:00.179
Doctor Strange gives up the Time Stone to
save Tony's life, leaving Thanos to quickly

00:14:00.180 --> 00:14:03.780
complete his Infinity Gauntlet and snap half
the universe into non-existence.

00:14:03.960 --> 00:14:08.499
Tony survives, but Peter Parker turns to dust
in his arms, and only he and Nebula are left

00:14:08.500 --> 00:14:10.940
alive on Titan, seemingly with no way home.

00:14:11.480 --> 00:14:16.079
After Thanos' devastating victory, Nebula
and Tony leave Titan in Quill's ship, but

00:14:16.080 --> 00:14:19.060
they don't have the supplies or the fuel to
actually make it all the way back to Earth.

00:14:19.220 --> 00:14:23.220
Carol Danvers, a.k.a. Captain Marvel, intercepts
their ship and gives them a lift home.

00:14:23.380 --> 00:14:28.020
Once he arrives, Tony realizes that his 50/50
odds of everyone in his life surviving came

00:14:28.020 --> 00:14:31.560
out pretty well: Pepper, Happy, and Rhodey
all survived the Snap.

00:14:31.800 --> 00:14:35.400
For the next five years, the only thing on
Tony's mind is building a life for himself,

00:14:35.720 --> 00:14:39.639
Pepper, and their young daughter Morgan, as
Tony finally manages to retire the way he

00:14:39.640 --> 00:14:40.790
kept promising he would.

00:14:40.900 --> 00:14:45.000
Or at least he retires until Scott Lang reappears
from the Quantum Realm with a theory that

00:14:45.009 --> 00:14:48.179
they could go back in time and save everyone
who died because of Thanos.

00:14:48.179 --> 00:14:52.769
"What if there was a way that we could enter
the quantum realm at a certain point in time,

00:14:52.769 --> 00:14:55.040
but then exit the quantum realm at another
point in time and exit in a certain point

00:14:55.040 --> 00:14:55.540
in time?

00:14:56.040 --> 00:14:57.040
like… like before Thanos."

00:14:57.300 --> 00:15:01.360
After some hemming and hawing, Tony builds
a working time machine model, rejoins the

00:15:01.369 --> 00:15:05.699
Avengers, returns Cap's shield, and organizes
a strike team of the surviving Avengers to

00:15:05.699 --> 00:15:10.049
go back in time to retrieve the Infinity Stones
and build a new gauntlet before Thanos destroys

00:15:10.049 --> 00:15:10.840
them in the present.

00:15:11.089 --> 00:15:14.600
The mission goes smoothly, and Tony even gets
a chance to have a heart-to-heart with his

00:15:14.600 --> 00:15:15.520
dad in the past.

00:15:15.960 --> 00:15:18.800
"Howard… everything's gonna be alright.

00:15:20.760 --> 00:15:24.160
Thank you… for everything."

00:15:24.600 --> 00:15:28.360
From there, all it takes is one snap of Hulk's
mighty fingers to bring everyone back.

00:15:28.540 --> 00:15:33.060
However, a past version of Thanos battles
his way to the future, and only Tony Stark,

00:15:33.060 --> 00:15:36.980
by sacrificing his life to use a new Infinity
Gauntlet, can finally get rid of him.

00:15:38.120 --> 00:15:42.460
Tony Stark gives his life to erase Thanos
and his world-conquering army from the past,

00:15:42.460 --> 00:15:45.540
finally making good on Ho Yinsen's plea that
he not waste his own life.

00:15:45.780 --> 00:15:48.120
He dies, and most of the MCU lives on.

00:15:48.240 --> 00:15:51.980
But just because Tony Stark dies doesn't mean
that his story dies with him; Tony leaves

00:15:51.980 --> 00:15:55.300
three extremely qualified members of the next
generation to succeed him.

00:15:55.360 --> 00:15:59.900
His daughter, Morgan Stark, takes after him
in a number of ways, and a genius-level intellect

00:15:59.900 --> 00:16:01.080
seems to run in the family.

00:16:01.249 --> 00:16:05.900
His young mentee, Peter Parker, grew up with
a hero worship of Tony Stark and spends most

00:16:05.900 --> 00:16:09.160
of Spider-Man: Far from Home trying to live
up to the legend of Iron Man.

00:16:09.280 --> 00:16:13.820
Finally, Harley Keener, the young boy that
Tony related to in Iron Man 3, appears at

00:16:13.829 --> 00:16:17.600
Tony's funeral, signifying that the Marvel
Cinematic Universe hasn't forgotten Tony's

00:16:17.600 --> 00:16:18.780
first young protégé.

00:16:18.780 --> 00:16:22.440
Even before the next generation is able to
take on the weight of the legacy he leaves

00:16:22.449 --> 00:16:25.929
them, Rhodey and Pepper both have high-tech
battle suits and a knack for doing the right

00:16:25.929 --> 00:16:26.420
thing.

00:16:26.420 --> 00:16:30.020
Just because Tony Stark has passed into the
great beyond doesn't mean that the legacy

00:16:30.029 --> 00:16:33.649
of Iron Man won't continue to reverberate
throughout the MCU going forward.

00:16:33.649 --> 00:16:35.720
And remember: There's no need to cry for Tony.

00:16:35.820 --> 00:16:37.000
He knew the hero gig:

00:16:37.500 --> 00:16:38.840
"Part of the journey is the end."

